when I heard of the the building of  fiber-to-the-home in Sweden the first  thing I thought of was finally I thought  this was the way for my dreams to come  through Aachen Karlsson is a Swedish  film editor who spent years editing  movies during which sunlight was a rare  pleasure and being able to work from  home was a dream many light-years away  but when ftth came to the small village  of Shilla for north of Stockholm Hawken  decided to transform this 19th century  schoolhouse into an editing studio  allowing his dream to become reality  now when I have the fibre to my doorstep  it's possible for me to live completely  another lives than before I mean earlier  I spend 12 14 hours a day seven days a  week and during that time I don't see my  family that much that's for sure  sometimes I need and not in the same  serious to my family thanks to fiber and  the dream of working from home  pakkun Carlson invented a revolutionary  editing tool an internet-based system  called Hawkeye it allows film editors to  work remotely and eliminates the use of  transportation today I can work remotely  with my editing to earlier we have to  fly if producers or directors from  Berlin some 800 kilometers to Stockholm  or from Oslo some 450 kilometers to  Stockholm just to view a version of a  film and today through the hawk eye we  can see the the streaming video instead  of attending or shipping DVDs so we  saved a lot of time and thereby a lot of  money and we also protected the  environment I don't think I actually  really left my editing room when I  worked in Stockholm and nowadays I have  the nature close to my house in my  office so I can have a walk by the lake  or somewhere and not actually thinking  about my job and things but when I come  back to the office I have solved things  during my walk I would say  I am thanks to the fiber-to-the-home I  can end my day almost whenever I want to  I don't have to finish things before I  can go home I can just leave them go  home and eat dinner with my family and  then hook up from my laptop at home and  continue wherever I were before  now the way I work today I'm more  efficient I can be wherever I want to be  and we can still do the same things now  my assistant can be in Stockholm which  is 250 kilometers from here and just log  into my computer or do things together  with me and help me out the support of  hawk which is 500 kilometers up north  can log-in and help me out with problems  with the avid or something I could also  have collaborations with directors in  Stockholm or producers in Stockholm  the fibre to the home and didn't made my  home closer it made my work closer  you
 

